  "rationale": "The target crownData:exfiltrate is an OR over codeRepo, dbReplica, shareMount and vaultRead. codeRepo:collection alone has redundant routes, so no single block cuts it. Route 1 is monitoringHost:lateralMovement, which is an OR over configSecret, ssoLogin and dbLogin. configSecret itself is reachable from vpnGateway (a foothold) or ciRunner. Route 2 is jumpHost:lateralMovement via dbLogin, which needs mailClient AND configSecret. Each candidate block leaves a path open. Blocking monitoringHost leaves jumpHost to codeRepo. Blocking jumpHost or dbLogin leaves configSecret to monitoringHost to codeRepo. Blocking configSecret leaves ssoLogin (ciRunner AND tokenCache, both reachable) to monitoringHost to codeRepo. Blocking ciRunner leaves vpnGateway to configSecret to monitoringHost to codeRepo. Blocking mailClient leaves configSecret to monitoringHost. Every other step is not on the codeRepo route at all. Therefore no single non-foothold step is a chokepoint."
 },
